Return `false` from the `_.transform` callback to stop iteration early. Mutate the accumulator before returning:

```js
_.transform([2, 3, 4], function (result, n) {
  result.push(n * n);
  return n % 2 === 0; // false stops iteration
}, []);

// => [4, 9]
```

The callback receives `(accumulator, value, key, object)`. The returned value is used as a continuation flag, so returning values such as a replacement accumulator does not replace the accumulator; mutate it in place instead.
